course: dictionary
lesson: 8394
title: Rudely: bad manners and sudden shocks
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Rudely is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It means in a way that is not polite and shows no respect for other people. Read «A girl in Dublin spoke rudely to a bus driver; he still helped her when she got on the wrong bus, and she felt ashamed and said sorry.» The clues show that speaking rudely is bad manners, and that is why she had to say sorry.
explain: Rudely can also mean suddenly and unpleasantly. «The alarm rudely woke him» does not mean the alarm was impolite. It means the alarm woke him up suddenly, and that was unpleasant. This is the meaning in «rudely awakened».
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. In «Toad, not really listening, jokes rudely that he has several aunts», does "without respect" make sense? Yes, so that is the meaning here.
fact: Rudely is an adverb: rudely, more rudely, most rudely.
fact: «Rudely» means in a way that is not polite and shows no respect for others.
fact: «Rudely» can also mean suddenly and unpleasantly, as in «rudely awakened».
fact: Useful phrases are rudely interrupt, speak rudely, and rudely awakened.
fact: When a teacher tells you off, do not answer back rudely; listen and say sorry if you were wrong.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin spoke rudely to a bus driver.» How did she speak? | Very quietly and kindly | *Without respect, in a way that is not polite | Happily, with a big smile | Slowly, so he could hear every word
exercise: «The alarm rudely woke him.» What does rudely mean here? | *Suddenly and unpleasantly | Politely, with a smile | Very gently and slowly
exercise: Which action is done rudely? | *Interrupting someone who is still talking | Waiting your turn to speak | Listening carefully to your teacher | Saying please and thank you
test: «Toad jokes rudely that he has several aunts who ought to be washerwomen.» Why is the joke rude? | Toad shows no respect for the gaoler's daughter | *Toad says something unkind without thinking of her feelings | Toad is thanking her for a gift | Toad is telling a sad true story
test: Which word is the best swap for rudely in «He spoke rudely»? | Gently | Sadly | *Impolitely | Carefully
exam: When a teacher tells you off, what should you do? | Answer back rudely | Walk out of the room | Laugh at the teacher | *Listen, say sorry if you were wrong, and do not answer back rudely
